---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The PHV Prep UK Android Test Is Underway — Launch Expected 18 August"
  description="PHV Prep UK has started its 14-day Google Play closed test. If all goes well, the Android version launches on 18 August 2026."
  image="/images/android-beta-testers.png"
>
  <main class="md:flex md:justify-center">
    <article class="prose prose-lg max-w-[750px]">
      <img
        src="/images/android-beta-testers.png"
        alt="PHV Prep UK Android closed testing is underway"
        width="1200"
        height="630"
        class="rounded-lg"
      />

      <h1>
        The PHV Prep UK Android Test Is Underway — Launch Expected 18 August
      </h1>

      <p>
        We've reached a big milestone. PHV Prep UK has enough Android testers to
        begin Google's required 14-day closed testing period — the final step
        before the app can go live on the Google Play Store.
      </p>

      <p>
        If everything goes smoothly, the Android version of PHV Prep UK will
        launch on 18 August 2026, joining the iOS version that's already on the
        App Store.
      </p>

      <h2>A thank you</h2>

      <p>
        This step wouldn't have happened without the people who volunteered to
        test. A genuine thank you to the friends, contacts, and the Reddit
        testing community who stepped in and opted into the beta. Getting a
        niche app in front of the right testers is harder than it sounds, and
        every single person made a difference.
      </p>

      <h2>Testing communities worth knowing</h2>

      <p>
        If you're a developer facing the same closed-testing requirement, these
        Reddit communities are a real help for finding testers and testing other
        apps in return:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://www.reddit.com/r/AndroidAppTesters/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener">r/AndroidAppTesters</a
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://www.reddit.com/r/TestersCommunity/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener">r/TestersCommunity</a
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://www.reddit.com/r/AndroidTesting/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener">r/AndroidTesting</a
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://www.reddit.com/r/GooglePlayClosedTest/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener">r/GooglePlayClosedTest</a
          >
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        The culture in these groups is reciprocal — you test someone's app, they
        test yours. It's how we got here.
      </p>

      <h2>What happens next</h2>

      <p>
        The testers keep the app installed for the 14 days, and on 18 August we
        apply for production access. Once approved, PHV Prep UK will be
        available to every Android user searching for a way to pass the
        Wolverhampton private hire test.
      </p>

      <p>We'll post again the moment it's live.</p>

      <hr />

      <p>
        PHV Prep UK is built specifically for the Wolverhampton private hire
        (taxi badge) test. One payment, lifetime access — no subscription.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
